## 3. Adjustments: histogram, height and channel mixer (7 sections, 11 October 2026)

Filters index: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/node-library/filters/filters (11 October 2026)

### 3.1 Histogram Range (11 October 2026)

- Category: Filters, Adjustments. (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: reduces and/or moves the range of a grayscale input, remapping its transitions. (11 October 2026)
- Main parameters: "Range" (Numeric 0.0 to 1.0, default not stated, reduces the range like moving the Levels min and max inward); "Position" (Numeric 0.0 to 1.0, default not stated, offsets the reduction and sets a different midpoint). (11 October 2026)
- Notes: the page points to Histogram Scan as the more useful remap. (11 October 2026)
- Copernicus nearest: `Cop remap` (rescales values from one range to another). Status: documented_only. (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/node-library/filters/adjustments/histogram-range (11 October 2026)

### 3.2 Histogram Scan (11 October 2026)

- Category: Filters, Adjustments. (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: remaps the contrast and brightness of a grayscale input, and can grow or shrink masks. (11 October 2026)
- Main parameters: "Position" (Number 0.0 to 1.0, shifts the midpoint like brightness; default 0 gives all black, the page suggests about 0.5); "Contrast" (Number 0.0 to 1.0, sets how hard the transition is; default not stated); "Invert Position" (Boolean, inverts the result). (11 October 2026)
- Copernicus nearest: `Cop remap` (its threshold makes a soft or hard step around a midpoint). Status: documented_only. (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/node-library/filters/adjustments/histogram-scan (11 October 2026)

### 3.3 Histogram Scan Non-Uniform (11 October 2026)

- Category: Filters, Adjustments. (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: applies the Histogram Scan effect per pixel, driven by maps, instead of uniformly over the image. (11 October 2026)
- Inputs: "Input" (grayscale, source result); "Position Map" (grayscale, active only when "Use Position Input" is True); "Contrast Map" (grayscale, active only when "Use Contrast Input" is True). (11 October 2026)
- Main parameters: "Use Position Input" (Boolean); "position" (0.0 to 1.0); "Use Contrast Input" (Boolean); "contrast" (0.0 to 1.0). Defaults not stated. (11 October 2026)
- Notes: the page says it is more complex than Histogram Scan, so learn that node first. (11 October 2026)
- Copernicus nearest: `Cop remap` (partial: remap has no per-pixel control maps in this sense). Status: documented_only. (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/node-library/filters/adjustments/histogram-scan-non-uniform (11 October 2026)

### 3.4 Histogram Select (11 October 2026)

- Category: Filters, Adjustments. (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: selects a range of grayscale values centred on a chosen position, with the selection fading out around that range. (11 October 2026)
- Main parameters: "Position" (0.0 to 1.0, centre of the range); "Range" (0.0 to 1.0, width of the range); "Contrast" (0.0 to 1.0, sharpens the edges of the selection). Defaults not stated. (11 October 2026)
- Copernicus nearest: `Cop remap` (partial: remap gives one threshold step, while a band needs `Cop segmentbyvalue` and `Cop idtomask`). Status: documented_only. (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/node-library/filters/adjustments/histogram-select (11 October 2026)

### 3.5 Histogram Shift (11 October 2026)

- Category: Filters, Adjustments. (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: shifts the whole tonal range of an image by a set amount, wrapping values past the range limits back to the other end. (11 October 2026)
- Main parameters: "Position" (0.0 to 1.0, type and default not stated). A Position of 1.0 gives the same result as 0.0. (11 October 2026)
- Copernicus nearest: none. No Copernicus layer node wraps values around the range. Status: documented_only. (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/node-library/filters/adjustments/histogram-shift (11 October 2026)

